Subject: Inlines the compare-and-branch and equality fast paths so the generic compare helper is reached only when a coercion is unavoidable

What this does
  Inlines the compare-and-branch and equality fast paths so the generic compare helper is reached only when a coercion is unavoidable.

Why we need it
  `instanceof`, loose `==` and relational-on-objects - because the twelve fused compare-and-branch handlers inlined only both-int and both-float64.

What it adds
  `regvm_strict_eq`, `regvm_loose_eq`, `regvm_int_bit_truthy` (AND/OR/XOR/SHL/SAR/SHR zero test), `regvm_instanceof_fast` (ordinary `instanceof` when `b`'s prototype is `Function.prototype` and it has no `Symbol.hasInstance`), and a macro arm order of both-int, float, mixed int/double, strict-eq, loose-eq, instanceof, bit; `regvm_cmp_take` gains a strict-eq fast path and EQ/NEQ on numbers in `regvm_double_cmp`/`regvm_num_fast`; `QJS_REGVM_COUNT` sub/tag/pair histograms report what still reaches the helper.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  No.
